    "description": "PolicyDecisionService evaluates access requests by reading tenant claims and asking ClassificationClient.classify(documentId) for a document classification. PUBLIC must produce ALLOW, UNKNOWN must produce REVIEW, and RESTRICTED must produce DENY. The production client calls a licensed scanning service that is unavailable in CI, charges per request, and cannot reliably be induced to return every classification or fail on demand. A security test must cover all three decisions plus a timeout from the classifier, while assertions remain focused on the PolicyDecision returned by evaluate. The request identifier passed to the classifier is incidental and does not need to be constrained. Decide how the test should control the classifier's successful and exceptional responses without depending on the remote service.",
    "decision_statement": "Whether to replace the remote classifier with a test-specific responder that returns selected classifications and raises selected failures to drive each policy branch.",
    "notes": "The remote classifier is replaced with a responder returning selected classifications and failures to drive each policy branch (stub); configurable-test-double is the near-miss for reusable per-test configuration."
